# =============================================================================
# STANDING RULE: GitHub carries the SHIPPED GAME and nothing else.
#
# No planning documents. No idea documents. No design docs, specs, research
# notes, knowledge maps, allocation tables, brainstorms, meeting notes, drafts,
# handoff scratch or review screenshots. Ever.
#
# Those live on disk and in the Obsidian vault, which is where thinking belongs.
# The repo is for files the game needs to run, plus the minimum documentation
# needed to pick the code back up.
#
# When adding a new file, ask: does the game need this to run, or does a
# developer need it to understand what shipped? If neither, it is ignored here
# BEFORE the first commit.
#
# Currently kept on GitHub: README.md, GAME-OVERVIEW.md (what shipped),
# game/README.md, game/COVERAGE.md, game/EDITOR.md, and game/ itself.
# =============================================================================

